  "report": "Implementation review passed; operator acceptance remains separate.\n\nACCEPT. OBSERVED: the current hashes of `pass.rs` and `pass_tests.rs` match the supplied candidate checkpoint; `git status` contains only the four allocated paths and `git diff --check` passes. SD-R-001 is closed: the single local `takes_part` predicate excludes a genuine forward declaration both while indexing candidate enclosing types and while selecting METHOD recipients. The added C++ prototype fixture proves that the `c.h` prototype keeps its previous document/hash while the `c.cc` definition receives the class sentence.\n\nOBSERVED witness: FRAKTAG `ConversationManager.ts` documents `ConversationManager handles conversation persistence.`, defines `createSession` at line 71 and `logTurn` at line 133. The after capture renders `ConversationManager.createSession` at rank 8, score 0.333; the before capture has no such row. OBSERVED leveldb capture retains `leveldb::Iter::CorruptionError` at `table/block.cc:242` (0.398), `leveldb::RepairDB` at `db/repair.cc:446` (0.333), and `leveldb_repair_db` at `db/c.cc:278` (0.301). This supplies the ratified bounded Layer-3 hint without changing deterministic ranking, tiers, model, storage, or CLI surfaces, supporting the VISION's task-oriented orientation."
